 ("chapter", "|The Book We Still Do Not Have", "dore_020"),
 ("vo", "So where is the real Book of Jasher? The plain answer is that it is lost. What survives are two short poems, and perhaps a third. Joshua's command to the sun, and David's lament for Saul and Jonathan.", "dore_020"),
 ("vo", "The books that carry its name today are something else: a medieval retelling from Italy, and an English hoax. Neither is the book that Joshua's writer expected his readers to open.", "dore_031"),
 ("vo", "Was it a book of songs, sung long before Israel had kings? Or a royal record kept in the temple? Unless it turns up one day, like the Dead Sea Scrolls, in a cave, we may never know.", "rd_204"),
